```java
import com.sun.jna.*;
import com.sun.jna.platform.win32.WinBase;
import com.sun.jna.platform.win32.WinNT;
import com.sun.jna.ptr.PointerByReference;

public interface MoreAdvapi32 extends StdCallLibrary {
    MoreAdvapi32 INSTANCE = Native.load("Advapi32", MoreAdvapi32.class, W32APIOptions.UNICODE_OPTIONS);

    boolean CreateProcessWithTokenW(WinNT.HANDLE hToken, int dwLogonFlags,
                                    String lpApplicationName, String lpCommandLine,
                                    int dwCreationFlags, Pointer lpEnvironment,
                                    String lpCurrentDirectory, WinBase.STARTUPINFO lpStartupInfo,
                                    WinBase.PROCESS_INFORMATION lpProcessInformation);
}

public class Example {
    public static void main(String... args) {
        String appPath = "Path to your exe";
        WinNT.HANDLEByReference hToken = new WinNT.HANDLEByReference();
        WinBase.STARTUPINFO startupInfo = new WinBase.STARTUPINFO();
        WinBase.PROCESS_INFORMATION processInformation = new WinBase.PROCESS_INFORMATION();
        PointerByReference lpEnvironment = null;

        // Populate hToken, startupInfo, processInformation and lpEnvironment as needed...

        boolean result = MoreAdvapi32.INSTANCE.CreateProcessWithTokenW(
                hToken.getValue(),
                0,          // Flags
                appPath,
                null,       // Command line options
                0,          // Creation flags
                lpEnvironment.getValue(),
                null,       // Current directory
                startupInfo,
                processInformation
        );

        // Process the result...
    }
}
```

Here, we manually loaded Advapi32.dll, which includes CreateProcessWithTokenW, and directly mapped it using JNA. You'll need to expand on this example to suit your needs (like proper exception handling, error checking, populating the structures etc.). 

Note that CreateProcessWithTokenW requires the SE_IMPERSONATE_NAME privilege to be enabled in the calling process, and that privilege is not typically granted to non-administrative users.

Also realize that CreateProcessWithTokenW is fairly complex with various inputs and outputs and the exact way you use it can significantly vary depending on your requirements. It might require some reading and experimenting on your part if you're not already familiar with it.

