In this script, 'is_prime' function checks if a number is prime. 'is_mersenne_number' function checks if a number is in Mersenne's form (2^P-1) and 'is_mersenne_prime' function checks if a number is a Mersenne prime i.e. both prime and a Mersenne number. 'gcd' is a recursive function that calculates the Greatest Common Divisor (GCD) of two numbers using the Euclidean algorithm.

However, please note this solution is not optimized for very large integers as checking for prime numbers is a computationally intensive operation. Also, checking if a number is a Mersenne number also involves iteratively computing the series 2^P-1 until the computed number is not less than the input, which can itself be a costly operation for large inputs.

